WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:17.784 --> 00:00:20.253
Hello everyone.

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:23.223
Just came back from a little holiday.

00:00:24.958 --> 00:00:26.626
So this is not a normal video,

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:29.629
but I do a Q and A.

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:34.534
I just came back from, Sardinia. Ela was there the week before

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:37.637
to shoot a documentary

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:39.572
about,

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:46.312
heritage clothing
and traditional dress from Sardinia and Romania,
where her family is from.

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:50.717
So added a little holiday, so

00:00:51.351 --> 00:00:53.286
that's where we were this week.

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:54.354
I've been pointing today.

00:00:54.354 --> 00:00:57.190
My brother's here and a friend,

00:00:57.190 --> 00:01:00.193
We just finished the wall, but the work...

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:01.494
That we did today,

00:01:01.494 --> 00:01:03.463
Worked on the solar panels as well.

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:06.299
I'll add that in next week's video.

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:08.268
So I did a post,

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:10.403
see what people's questions were.

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:14.074
I do a Q&amp;A once in a while,
but it's been a while, so.

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:19.212
Let's see.

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:31.091
Could you update us on the second cabin?

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:31.958
Yeah.

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:33.526
Ela is cleaning it up right now, actually

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:36.529
to make it her workspace
for the time being.

00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:39.666
I have some more work
to do on the workshop,

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:45.438
but I do want to do the roof this summer.

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:47.073
To have that done before winter.

00:01:47.073 --> 00:01:50.710
Because working on the roof on
the workshop was quite difficult.

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:52.412
It's doable...

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:59.452
But, clearing
all the snow, it's makes more sense to do something like that in the in the summer.

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:03.490
So I think in a few weeks,
I will start there again.

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:06.493
I made a start there with the bathroom
work.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:10.463
Last year and in the winter,

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:14.000
when I was waiting for the paperwork
to be finished for the workshop at once,

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:14.701
When that was all done.

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:17.070
The priority was
to get the workshop finished.

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:22.208
And we get there slowly.

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:23.943
There's still a lot of work
to be done inside.

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:26.980
And I think through winter
it will be easier

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:29.983
to do inside work when the heating is on.

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:31.951
You know, and the days are short.

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:36.656
It will be more pleasant to work inside
to finish the workshop.

00:02:37.357 --> 00:02:40.860
but it will be great
when the roof is also done for the,

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:44.230
for the second cabin.

00:02:45.098 --> 00:02:51.137
Does the tank behind the wood stove work well?

00:02:51.137 --> 00:02:53.640
Yeah, it works great, actually.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:03:00.413
We're we're fully relying on the on the water
tank behind the stove in the winter.

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:05.385
Now, about six weeks ago,
I looped it through to the electric boiler

00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:08.488
because we still make fires,
but they're quite a lot smaller.

00:03:08.488 --> 00:03:11.524
So the the water in the tank
doesn't get that hot.

00:03:12.292 --> 00:03:13.760
So before it goes,

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:19.899
to the taps, it goes through the electric boiler
where it's heated up to full.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:21.901
And it works really well.

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:27.840
But most of the winter, I think until late
March, we were using the water tank,

00:03:28.841 --> 00:03:31.844
gets up to 60 Cº or so,

00:03:32.345 --> 00:03:34.681
really, depending on how big

00:03:34.681 --> 00:03:37.684
we make the fires. And,

00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:39.252
Yeah, it took a while.

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:45.225
You can see in... well I can't remember
which videos, we were struggling a bit

00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:48.595
in the beginning, but now the design is
good and it's working properly.

00:03:55.168 --> 00:04:00.740
Why did you decide not to put a skylight in the workshop roof?

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:05.345
It was not approved by planning permission,
so I couldn't put it in there.

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:09.249
It's classified as a garage, basically.

00:04:09.249 --> 00:04:11.618
So, Yeah.

00:04:11.618 --> 00:04:12.151
It's fine.

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:16.089
There's enough light coming in through
the front door, which are quite big.

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:18.391
If you open those up fully.

00:04:18.391 --> 00:04:22.729
And, the other two little windows
and the one in the back, it's light enough.

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:25.698
But obviously
the workshop needs a lot of light,

00:04:25.698 --> 00:04:29.035
so there's going to be lights everywhere
above the work tables.

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:33.873
So I'll
be working on that in the coming weeks.

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:36.643
I think I shared a design

00:04:36.643 --> 00:04:38.711
some time ago, like an early rendering

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:41.714
 of the inside of the workshop.

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:44.150
As I mentioned earlier, it's
going to be like

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:48.721
a little working station in the center
where I do most of the work

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:52.659
with a workbench, table saw
and an outfeed table.

00:04:52.659 --> 00:04:56.763
And all around it there will be,
workbenches as well, and storage

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:59.132
all on one level.

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:03.703
I don't think higher cabinet, but things
will be hanging on the wall as well

00:05:04.404 --> 00:05:07.407
that I would need on a day to day basis.

00:05:07.974 --> 00:05:10.276
Things that are nice to store on the wall,

00:05:10.276 --> 00:05:13.279
like hand tools, for example.

00:05:13.813 --> 00:05:15.148
But yeah, more

00:05:15.148 --> 00:05:17.884
designs and plans I will share later.

00:05:17.884 --> 00:05:22.322
And I think the interior work of the
workshop, which is still a lot of work,

00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:25.258
if I'm going to make cabinetry by myself,

00:05:26.693 --> 00:05:30.930
this is probably a nice winter project to do.

00:05:32.432 --> 00:05:39.105
When all the major construction and renovation work is done, what do you envision will be come the main objective of your channel

00:05:39.105 --> 00:05:42.108
Yeah, it's a good question.

00:05:42.942 --> 00:05:43.476
I don't know.

00:05:43.476 --> 00:05:46.713
the question is, when is all the work done?

00:05:47.246 --> 00:05:50.283
I can imagine
when both cabins in the workshop is done,

00:05:50.817 --> 00:05:53.820
the next thing would be
the front door of the first cabin.

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:54.687
Which is not that good.

00:05:54.687 --> 00:05:57.223
 I'll redo some jobs.

00:05:57.223 --> 00:05:58.691
I'll get into woodworking.

00:05:58.691 --> 00:06:01.694
Maybe more painting.

00:06:01.861 --> 00:06:05.732
Landscaping, definitely.

00:06:05.732 --> 00:06:06.332
Like the.

00:06:06.332 --> 00:06:12.271
The primary goal is now
to get the construction work and then the three buildings finished.

00:06:12.939 --> 00:06:19.112
But I see there are kind of like five stages in this bigger projects.

00:06:19.645 --> 00:06:22.482
The first one being

00:06:22.482 --> 00:06:25.685
establishing a livable area,
basically.

00:06:25.685 --> 00:06:30.156
So installation of solar panels
and getting electricity and power,

00:06:31.624 --> 00:06:35.528
creating taps and the water connection,

00:06:35.528 --> 00:06:38.531
which was there, but it was a lot of work to make
it work.

00:06:38.731 --> 00:06:42.301
Pipes underground and trenching
and setting up the tent area.

00:06:43.236 --> 00:06:45.838
So that was the first
year, half a year or so.

00:06:47.507 --> 00:06:50.276
So I had a comfortable situation
with the outdoor kitchen and shower

00:06:50.276 --> 00:06:53.846
to live there
and then work on the first cabin,

00:06:54.447 --> 00:06:57.316
which is the second project,
finishing the first cabin

00:06:57.316 --> 00:07:01.621
and have a permanent living situation
like a comfortable heated space

00:07:03.222 --> 00:07:05.792
also in the winter.

00:07:05.792 --> 00:07:08.528
That was done after two years

00:07:08.528 --> 00:07:11.531
or so, a little bit more maybe.

00:07:11.731 --> 00:07:13.866
And then

00:07:13.866 --> 00:07:16.869
2nd Cabin is the third project,

00:07:17.036 --> 00:07:19.372
and the 4th project being the workshop.

00:07:19.372 --> 00:07:23.443
They kind of are coming along simultaneously.

00:07:23.443 --> 00:07:28.414
I've done some work on the 2nd cabin, in the basement.

00:07:28.748 --> 00:07:31.751
Now the priority is to get the workshop
finished.

00:07:32.218 --> 00:07:36.489
And then once all of that is done,
landscaping is the bigger project

00:07:36.489 --> 00:07:40.760
for a longer future,
you know, building terrace walls,

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:44.564
stairs, like the stairway
in between the two cabins.

00:07:45.798 --> 00:07:48.801
Garden beds in stone,

00:07:49.802 --> 00:07:51.237
Making the road better,

00:07:51.237 --> 00:07:52.505
Just everything outside.

00:07:52.505 --> 00:07:55.508
There's a lot of potential there,
you know, a gate.

00:07:56.108 --> 00:07:58.778
Fencing needs to be finished.

00:07:58.778 --> 00:08:01.714
There's a lot to do
and to make everything really beautiful,

00:08:01.714 --> 00:08:03.850
because it's really messy around the workshop
right now.

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:08.588
 it's a construction site,
you know, the soil is all broken up.

00:08:08.588 --> 00:08:10.323
Nothing is growing there.

00:08:10.323 --> 00:08:12.225
You know, seeding grass and plants.

00:08:12.225 --> 00:08:18.931
There's a lot of potential,
I think, there to make the place visually from the outside really beautiful.

00:08:18.931 --> 00:08:21.934
Once everything is working inside.

00:08:24.003 --> 00:08:25.872
And that could take could take years.

00:08:26.739 --> 00:08:29.742
It's kind of an endless job
to maintain the site.

00:08:30.109 --> 00:08:35.448
If you want to keep,
keep it looking beautiful, and clean.

00:08:35.448 --> 00:08:36.849
You'll be working on it every day.

00:08:38.284 --> 00:08:45.491
You mentioned plans to make a pond since there was a natural pond in the landscape. Do you still plan to create terraces and a pond?

00:08:45.491 --> 00:08:46.158
Yeah.

00:08:46.158 --> 00:08:50.329
A pond, so that is part of that 5th stage, basically

00:08:50.329 --> 00:08:54.433
a pond could be beautiful
there.

00:08:54.433 --> 00:08:55.501
Yeah, it's in the works.

00:08:55.501 --> 00:08:59.939
I mean, I need to spend some time
designing that, but it's really for later.

00:09:00.573 --> 00:09:03.776
I think it would be really beautiful
in the gardening area there.

00:09:04.210 --> 00:09:08.114
Like in front of the greenhouse
terracing, with garden baths

00:09:08.114 --> 00:09:11.751
and a pond could be part of that.

00:09:13.352 --> 00:09:16.355
Maybe a duck pond?

00:09:16.355 --> 00:09:18.057
Well, it's going to be very dirty.

00:09:18.057 --> 00:09:21.861
Ducks could be part
of the animal corner as well.

00:09:22.595 --> 00:09:25.631
They need some water, probably

00:09:26.432 --> 00:09:27.166
Yeah.

00:09:27.166 --> 00:09:30.169
It's far in the future.

00:09:31.704 --> 00:09:37.777
How did you come to constructing the workshop without licensed supervision?

00:09:37.777 --> 00:09:39.645
No, there is actually supervision.

00:09:39.645 --> 00:09:43.482
There's a, director of works,
geometra, architect.

00:09:43.482 --> 00:09:45.818
All those people are involved
to legally do this.

00:09:45.818 --> 00:09:49.088
You know, they sign off the project,
but they're not in the videos.

00:09:50.590 --> 00:09:57.430
What would you say to your 20-year-old self if you cold talk to him?

00:09:58.831 --> 00:10:00.566
I don't know... 

00:10:00.566 --> 00:10:03.569
what was I doing when I was 20 years old?

00:10:03.869 --> 00:10:09.875
I was studying graphic design in Eindhoven,
in the south of the Netherlands.

00:10:10.810 --> 00:10:13.879
I was playing in bands, writing music.

00:10:14.246 --> 00:10:17.283
was doing quite different
things, actually, from what I do now.

00:10:21.020 --> 00:10:21.621
Yeah.

00:10:21.621 --> 00:10:22.622
I was just on this road...

00:10:22.622 --> 00:10:25.691
You just choose as an education.

00:10:25.691 --> 00:10:27.360
I mean, you could just...

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:29.328
But you don't know
if that's going to be your life.

00:10:29.328 --> 00:10:32.131
But that was the goal
to become a graphic designer.

00:10:32.131 --> 00:10:35.134
And no the goal was to become a rock star.

00:10:35.601 --> 00:10:37.403
with a band.

00:10:37.403 --> 00:10:38.771
Didn't happen.

00:10:38.771 --> 00:10:40.940
But there was

00:10:40.940 --> 00:10:42.908
what I was at,

00:10:42.908 --> 00:10:44.410
actually around 20, 21...

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:47.880
It was the defining part of my life
and career.

00:10:47.880 --> 00:10:50.883
I would say I was studying graphic design,

00:10:51.083 --> 00:10:53.819
but it was not a great education.

00:10:53.819 --> 00:10:54.720
It was fine, but...

00:10:57.390 --> 00:11:00.192
I remember I had one good teacher

00:11:00.192 --> 00:11:03.195
and he, he really challenged me

00:11:03.896 --> 00:11:06.599
and kind of provoked me as well.

00:11:06.599 --> 00:11:10.169
I was struggling with him,
but he was actually helping me a lot

00:11:10.736 --> 00:11:13.739
and challenging me.

00:11:14.106 --> 00:11:16.242
And I think he liked my work.

00:11:16.242 --> 00:11:18.210
He was saying, like, you need to...

00:11:18.210 --> 00:11:21.213
Because it was the last year of my education

00:11:21.681 --> 00:11:25.985
He was saying
you have to work at this design firm

00:11:25.985 --> 00:11:29.655
in Amsterdam, it was like a big design firm,
that was based in London

00:11:30.356 --> 00:11:33.359
and had offices in Amsterdam and Singapore.

00:11:33.726 --> 00:11:38.064
And he said he knew the executive creative
director there.

00:11:38.431 --> 00:11:41.400
And he said, like,
I think you fit in perfectly there,

00:11:41.934 --> 00:11:44.937
so I'll write him
and then maybe you can get a job there

00:11:45.071 --> 00:11:48.074
as your first job after studying design.

00:11:48.908 --> 00:11:50.876
And I was very excited about that.

00:11:52.111 --> 00:11:54.413
And some time passed

00:11:54.413 --> 00:11:57.983
and I asked him a few times,
did you get in touch with them?

00:11:57.983 --> 00:12:00.986
And he said, like, yes...

00:12:01.153 --> 00:12:04.156
they said, it's
best if you just get in touch with...

00:12:05.091 --> 00:12:07.426
with reception or a regular email address

00:12:07.426 --> 00:12:11.964
on their website
and just write your portfolio and maybe,

00:12:12.531 --> 00:12:15.067
they invite you.

00:12:15.067 --> 00:12:17.670
So I did, and actually,
it was pretty random.

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:21.273
You know,
if you are at the start of your career,

00:12:21.874 --> 00:12:24.877
you might have a dream
where you could work

00:12:25.444 --> 00:12:29.949
and then, yeah, you might have a benchmark
which is quite high up there,

00:12:30.616 --> 00:12:32.952
because most of my peers,
that was were finishing

00:12:32.952 --> 00:12:37.156
they would go to a local design agency
in the south of the Netherlands,

00:12:38.224 --> 00:12:43.662
start there and climb up the ladder,
and then perhaps end up at,

00:12:44.930 --> 00:12:46.499
you know, a bigger firm.

00:12:46.499 --> 00:12:51.070
but I tried it anyway, trusting
that he would put in a good word for me.

00:12:51.570 --> 00:12:53.572
And I had,

00:12:53.572 --> 00:12:55.841
I showed my portfolio there

00:12:55.841 --> 00:12:59.145
to a creative director,
and eventually they offered me,

00:13:00.980 --> 00:13:04.316
sort of internship two-month contract.

00:13:04.316 --> 00:13:05.551
Where I worked in the summer there

00:13:05.551 --> 00:13:08.554
 and it went really well.

00:13:08.821 --> 00:13:11.824
And then they offered me
a more longer term contract.

00:13:13.659 --> 00:13:14.560
It was very scary.

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:16.162
It was all speaking English.

00:13:16.162 --> 00:13:18.030
My English was very bad at the time.

00:13:18.030 --> 00:13:20.933
I was 21, and I.

00:13:20.933 --> 00:13:23.936
But I asked about this teacher if,

00:13:26.038 --> 00:13:30.643
if he did actually some work and
I didn't know him at all, which is funny.

00:13:30.643 --> 00:13:32.645
So he he was kind of bluffing.

00:13:32.645 --> 00:13:34.280
He was pushing me in a direction.

00:13:34.280 --> 00:13:35.648
Okay, Martijn should go there

00:13:36.682 --> 00:13:40.319
On my own I would never have done that.

00:13:40.319 --> 00:13:43.322
But I'm glad it turned out like that
because it was a

00:13:43.789 --> 00:13:47.459
the best first job I could ever have in Amsterdam.

00:13:47.893 --> 00:13:50.129
Just as a start,
as a graphic design career.

00:13:50.129 --> 00:13:52.832
So I'm very happy with that.

00:13:52.832 --> 00:13:55.801
But it was
it was a it's a funny story that

00:13:56.435 --> 00:13:59.438
they didn't know him at all.

00:14:08.614 --> 00:14:18.624
Have you ever thought about setting up a camera looking out over the valley, or into the woods, in the rain or listening to the river or just hearing the birds and breeze, and letting it record for a few hours?

00:14:18.624 --> 00:14:21.627
Yeah, I think it wouldn't work

00:14:21.994 --> 00:14:24.997
because that's not how....

00:14:26.232 --> 00:14:27.499
How video works, cinema...

00:14:27.499 --> 00:14:30.236
Cinema is,

00:14:30.236 --> 00:14:31.837
it's a sequence of images

00:14:31.837 --> 00:14:37.476
and sound design and a choice
of how long you show something

00:14:37.476 --> 00:14:40.479
and what you show, what comes first
and what comes after

00:14:41.714 --> 00:14:46.085
I mean, if I could sit here
for half an hour enjoying my time here,

00:14:47.253 --> 00:14:53.859
but I wouldn't
just look at the view for that period in time,
you just start looking and then your eyes

00:14:53.859 --> 00:14:56.695
go to something else and then you see
a little insect somewhere,

00:14:58.030 --> 00:15:01.033
and you look at that and then.

00:15:01.533 --> 00:15:02.768
Feel something on your hand.

00:15:02.768 --> 00:15:05.838
You scratch your hand
and you figure out that your hands are dry

00:15:06.872 --> 00:15:09.174
and your thoughts go there.

00:15:09.174 --> 00:15:12.177
And I think it goes all over the place.

00:15:12.745 --> 00:15:16.649
And that's because you are here
in this space where there's a lot going on

00:15:17.516 --> 00:15:22.154
other than just one camera shot.

00:15:22.154 --> 00:15:26.358
I think it's much more, you feel the wind and the temperature.

00:15:26.358 --> 00:15:27.893
You smell things.

00:15:27.893 --> 00:15:29.194
You can look all around you.

00:15:29.194 --> 00:15:32.197
You have this 360 view.

00:15:34.233 --> 00:15:36.802
There's a few houses over there.

00:15:36.802 --> 00:15:39.805
There's a very deep crevice here.

00:15:40.306 --> 00:15:41.473
And this beautiful trees.

00:15:41.473 --> 00:15:43.976
So just one shot doesn't work.

00:15:43.976 --> 00:15:46.979
I think the videos are,

00:15:48.514 --> 00:15:52.384
like a long shot works. My videos are quite slow.

00:15:53.052 --> 00:15:57.356
Some shots are 20s, 30s sometimes.

00:15:57.356 --> 00:15:58.557
But something needs to happen.

00:16:02.428 --> 00:16:06.832
If there will be, like a farmer
with cows coming by through the valley,

00:16:07.900 --> 00:16:10.636
and I can have a shot of that,
that could take quite a while.

00:16:10.636 --> 00:16:13.205
It's nice to look at that,
but something needs to happen.

00:16:13.205 --> 00:16:16.008
A close up of a flower.

00:16:16.008 --> 00:16:19.645
You can look it out for 5-10s
and then it gets really boring.

00:16:19.645 --> 00:16:22.381
It needs to jump on to something else.

00:16:22.381 --> 00:16:23.716
And that's how videos work.

00:16:23.716 --> 00:16:26.719
I think it's it's really storytelling.

00:16:26.986 --> 00:16:31.023
And, it needs to have a certain rhythm.

00:16:31.023 --> 00:16:34.259
It can be a lot faster,
but then it's still every

00:16:34.259 --> 00:16:37.262
shot has a different length.

00:16:37.696 --> 00:16:40.399
So yeah.

00:16:40.399 --> 00:16:43.402
No, I think that doesn't work.

00:16:44.670 --> 00:16:50.309
What’s the first project in the workshop once it’s fully up and operational

00:16:50.309 --> 00:16:50.609
Well,

00:16:50.609 --> 00:16:53.879
probably, the front doors
and the back window,

00:16:54.079 --> 00:16:57.116
those are the first things that have to be
made to make it weatherproof.

00:16:57.316 --> 00:16:59.918
So I'll probably do that
in the workshop in a few weeks.

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:03.889
And from there it's,

00:17:03.889 --> 00:17:07.760
cabinetry and,
shelves and storage in the workshop.

00:17:07.760 --> 00:17:12.865
And then simultaneously,
I'll start work also, in the second cabin.

00:17:12.865 --> 00:17:15.868
So it's going to be front doors, windows,

00:17:16.502 --> 00:17:20.472
kitchen furniture, 

00:17:20.472 --> 00:17:21.607
flooring I don't know how I'm going to that yet,

00:17:21.607 --> 00:17:25.844
 all of that
is is more refined carpentry,

00:17:26.678 --> 00:17:29.648
that I want to spend more time
on than I did with the first cabin, like

00:17:29.648 --> 00:17:33.152
the first cabin was a living situation
I want to be in.

00:17:33.152 --> 00:17:37.222
I want to get inside quickly because I was
living in a tent at the time.

00:17:38.357 --> 00:17:41.693
And I think with building,
the second cabin is going to be more time

00:17:41.693 --> 00:17:44.696
into designing everything,

00:17:46.231 --> 00:17:48.600
building it properly, like better....

00:17:48.600 --> 00:17:50.502
I've learned a lot too, over the years.

00:17:52.271 --> 00:17:55.240
Wood carving, perhaps,

00:17:55.240 --> 00:17:56.942
include some of that.

00:17:56.942 --> 00:17:59.211
And, I'm really looking forward to that.

00:17:59.211 --> 00:18:02.614
And the workshop
is going to be an amazing place to do

00:18:02.614 --> 00:18:05.617
these kind of works in it, in a more

00:18:06.452 --> 00:18:11.223
professional way, just a higher level
than I and I could achieve before

00:18:11.223 --> 00:18:16.728
working at the workbench
outside, outdoors where it is right now.

00:18:19.098 --> 00:18:27.406
What’s your approach / philosophy to filming yourself? I’ve noticed how masterful &amp; intentional your sue of lighting is, how much work you put into changing angles, being mindful of focus to draw attention

00:18:27.406 --> 00:18:28.207
Well, it's

00:18:28.207 --> 00:18:31.210
yeah, it's
quite a simple set up of one camera,

00:18:33.812 --> 00:18:35.581
and a drone.

00:18:35.581 --> 00:18:38.083
I have more cameras,
but I only use one.

00:18:38.083 --> 00:18:44.690
It's just because they break
some time, so I have to  have another one ready.

00:18:44.690 --> 00:18:46.458
But I

00:18:46.458 --> 00:18:48.026
the great thing of this kind of work is

00:18:48.026 --> 00:18:51.964
if you are a creative person
or you make things,

00:18:52.831 --> 00:18:57.936
there's always the struggle
to decide for yourself when is something finished?

00:18:59.204 --> 00:19:01.640
With a painting, it's like that
with drawing,

00:19:01.640 --> 00:19:04.042
But with any work

00:19:04.042 --> 00:19:07.045
in making, it's like,
when is it good enough?

00:19:07.346 --> 00:19:10.682
And that's a personal choice

00:19:10.682 --> 00:19:11.884
for me it's quite straightforward.

00:19:11.884 --> 00:19:14.887
It's finished when it's Sunday.

00:19:15.487 --> 00:19:17.723
The video needs to be upload
and then it's ready.

00:19:17.723 --> 00:19:20.792
So I really enjoy being in this cycle.

00:19:20.826 --> 00:19:23.295
of every week making a video,

00:19:23.295 --> 00:19:25.831
I try to do it as best as possible,

00:19:25.831 --> 00:19:28.834
and it's really just life through my eyes.

00:19:29.134 --> 00:19:30.202
I start on Monday.

00:19:30.202 --> 00:19:33.205
All the videos are chronological.

00:19:34.173 --> 00:19:36.842
I start to work

00:19:36.842 --> 00:19:40.112
and depending on the weather, I film

00:19:40.412 --> 00:19:43.081
what I experience, what I see.

00:19:43.081 --> 00:19:44.316
If the weather is beautiful.

00:19:44.316 --> 00:19:46.118
if there’s a beautiful cloud sequence.

00:19:46.118 --> 00:19:48.620
I fly up the drone,

00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:51.790
I search for beautiful shots,
and that gets mixed

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:54.159
in with the work
that I'm doing at the time.

00:19:56.161 --> 00:19:56.995
And that's how it is.

00:19:56.995 --> 00:19:58.897
It goes very organically.

00:19:58.897 --> 00:20:03.068
I have a very fast workflow, as I'm
saying, with just one camera on a tripod,

00:20:04.203 --> 00:20:07.206
sometimes handheld. And,

00:20:07.806 --> 00:20:14.580
when I'm shooting,
I also know kind of exactly already how I'm editing it.

00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:15.981
And that's because

00:20:15.981 --> 00:20:19.885
I've done it so many times
now, this 209 videos.

00:20:19.885 --> 00:20:24.823
So it's a fast workflow and whatever I see
and what I find interesting,

00:20:24.823 --> 00:20:28.860
what makes me happy
or what makes me feel things, I film that

00:20:28.860 --> 00:20:33.465
in a way that I think fits
well for the videos, for other people

00:20:33.465 --> 00:20:37.603
to experience, is basically
what I see is always what you see as well.

00:20:38.103 --> 00:20:41.073
So yeah.

00:20:42.207 --> 00:20:46.011
What happened to the Pajero’s front fender?

00:20:46.011 --> 00:20:49.014
Yeah, I had a collision last year, 

00:20:49.181 --> 00:20:51.750
A while ago already, on the highway.

00:20:51.750 --> 00:20:55.721
It was a lot of traffic
and quite hectic at the time. And,

00:20:56.688 --> 00:20:57.189
someone was

00:20:57.189 --> 00:21:00.259
standing still with their car on the road,
and I didn't see them.

00:21:00.259 --> 00:21:02.494
One time I bumped into them.

00:21:02.494 --> 00:21:03.962
Nobody got hurt.

00:21:03.962 --> 00:21:06.331
It's just a car
wreck got wrecked a bit on the side a bit

00:21:06.331 --> 00:21:10.202
So I still have to replace,
those parts and,

00:21:11.803 --> 00:21:13.338
but, yeah, you know, it's

00:21:13.338 --> 00:21:16.541
always a rough drive here, so that's why
I'm holding back on repairing it.

00:21:18.243 --> 00:21:19.878
It gets scratches all the time

00:21:19.878 --> 00:21:22.881
here in the forest.

00:21:28.620 --> 00:21:28.920
Yeah.

00:21:28.920 --> 00:21:31.890
So finishing workshop, roughly,

00:21:33.992 --> 00:21:36.228
and then at some point, start building

00:21:36.228 --> 00:21:39.231
scaffolding for the second cabin
to do the roof.

00:21:40.532 --> 00:21:44.002
That scaffolding is going to be very much
in the way of where we are living.

00:21:44.002 --> 00:21:48.607
So that's so that's best
to do the roof in the summer

00:21:48.774 --> 00:21:52.311
or the end of the summer
and then before for the snow falls.

00:21:52.311 --> 00:21:54.479
That's all done and scaffolding can go away.

00:21:56.982 --> 00:21:58.550
That project takes a long time.

00:21:58.550 --> 00:22:02.220
If it's done in winter with short daylight
and just cleaning

00:22:02.220 --> 00:22:06.291
snow every time, like last winter was not
a it's not a good idea.

00:22:06.291 --> 00:22:09.294
It was fine at the time, but I mean...

00:22:10.262 --> 00:22:11.997
but so that's next.

00:22:11.997 --> 00:22:15.000
And then I come back to the workshop,
probably

00:22:15.734 --> 00:22:18.737
in autumn, working on the inside more.

00:22:19.171 --> 00:22:22.107
I'm going to build a woodstove in there
or and a chimney pipe

00:22:22.107 --> 00:22:25.110
so I can keep it warm and

00:22:25.110 --> 00:22:26.878
when the days are very, short coming

00:22:26.878 --> 00:22:29.881
winter, work inside and be comfortable.

00:22:30.816 --> 00:22:32.684
So yeah, workshop, second cabin.

00:22:32.684 --> 00:22:35.721
And then in a year or so,
second cabin, it's going to be

00:22:36.655 --> 00:22:37.923
no, it's not going to be finished.

00:22:37.923 --> 00:22:41.293
I think it's going to take another
two years to get things really finished up.

00:22:41.293 --> 00:22:42.294
But we'll see.

00:22:42.294 --> 00:22:46.064
I don't I don't plan these things much,
but I want to I just want

00:22:46.064 --> 00:22:46.832
to get the roof done.

00:22:48.066 --> 00:22:52.170
And but the first coming weeks
is solar panels finishing

00:22:52.170 --> 00:22:57.175
and do the floor of the workshop,
and then probably doors.

00:22:57.175 --> 00:23:01.480
It just needs to be waterproof
